          human: "Matgo is the quintessential two-player variant of 'Go-Stop', a popular Korean fishing game played with Hwatu ('Flower Cards'). Using a 48-card deck where each group of four represents a month/flower, players attempt to capture cards to form scoring combinations (Yaku). The name 'Matgo' distinguishes the 2-player competitive style from the 3-player 'Go-Stop'. It is arguably the most popular mobile and online game in South Korea.",
